## instruments
mutate.py was rebuilt once, before any arm was scored. The first version carried 20.2's shape —
hand-written per-arm (old, new) pairs — which puts a transcription step between an arm's code and
the edit applied to it. It now **derives** both mutations from each arm's own `server/store.js` by
an assertion-guarded substitution, and prints the literal pairs to `03c_arm_evidence.txt`, which is
what the hand table existed to provide.

Cross-check before trusting it: the derived pairs were compared against the published tables of
20.2 and 20.3. **12 of 12 prior arms match exactly, 0 mismatches.** That confirms the transform is
faithful and, in the other direction, that both published tables were right.

